From 18f515f339989e84543a27ebe3ac32ad25527962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:09:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Guardian G20: alert when the phone contacts a known
 stalkerware server

Data: Echap stalkerware-indicators (CC-BY 4.0), C2 domains only (not
vendors' marketing websites). tools/update_stalkerware.py pins the
source commit (git ls-remote) and refuses a truncated list; 993
domains (929 stalkerware, 64 watchware), 128 also listed as websites.

Core: SpywareDb matches a listed domain or its subdomains on label
boundaries; shared hosting platforms listed on their own are dropped
at load (none in the data). SpywareWatch alerts once per listed domain
per 6 h, keeps the last 20 alerts in memory only, thread safe.
SpywareDbTest 8 groups incl. the real list. Mutations (suffix match
without label boundary, no platform filter, no rate limit, no lock)
each fail a test; the concurrency test was tightened until removing
the lock failed it every run.

App: every query name (blocked or forwarded) is checked; a hit posts
a high-importance notification on a separate channel whose lock-screen
version only says "Guardian has a safety alert". Alert only, never
block (blocking can tip off whoever installed it). Watchware and
website-also domains get softer wording. Main screen: alert list with
safety advice, a standing line that no alert does not mean no
stalkerware, and the Echap attribution.

Emulator flow 4a2: look up a fresh subdomain of a listed C2 domain,
expect the notification and the in-app alert. CI runs SpywareDbTest.
App code not compiled locally (no Android SDK here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dphx7H7WfpCsybM6HswWFN
